WHAT THIS REGION DID NOT OBSERVE
  The engine's own repository was never queried for a definition total anywhere in
  this window, so no engine-side total exists in this capture.
  DEFINITIONS EXPECTED, FROM THE CORPUS        36
  DEFINITIONS LOADED, ENGINE REPOSITORY TOTAL  UNOBSERVED
  The second figure reads UNOBSERVED and not 36.  The two figures are reported
  separately precisely so that expected and observed stay separable, and copying
  the expected figure across into the observed one would destroy the only thing
  this file exists to establish.  An engine bean that constructs without throwing
  is not evidence that definitions loaded; only a count is, and this capture does
  not carry one.
  A live count could not be taken afterwards either.  Nothing is serving on the
  application port in this environment and three of the six reference services are
  not provisioned here at all.  Even had a count been obtainable, it would have
  come from a different boot than the byte-pinned window above, and splicing it in
  would have misrepresented the capture's provenance.  Recording UNOBSERVED is the
  honest outcome and it is consistent with the classification below.
  A related conflation is flagged so it is not read into this file.  A count of
  region lines that merely mention a definition file is not a count of definitions.
  This annotation reports the reconciliation figure of eight and the newly-deployed
  figure of zero, both observed, and reports the engine repository total as
  unobserved.  It asserts no other definition count.

RISK CLASSIFICATION
  RESIDUAL UNVERIFIED RISK, ASSIGNED TO THIS GATE, NOT CLEARED.
  The wording is deliberate and is not softened.  The workflow engine is the
  oldest load-bearing component in the reactor, a 2014-vintage release, and it
  could not be bootstrapped for testing in isolation without a database, so it was
  assigned to the deployment and smoke gates rather than declared safe.  Nothing
  in this capture may be read as verifying it, and nothing below reclassifies it.
  Its version is deliberately unchanged.  No compatibility failure was
  demonstrated for it, and a version change without a demonstrated compatibility
  reason is out of scope, so bumping the oldest load-bearing component in the
  reactor would itself be a rule violation and a far larger behavioural risk than
  the one this gate manages.  The honest corollary is stated with it, because the
  first half alone would flatter the result: not having demonstrated a failure is
  not the same as having demonstrated safety.  That gap is exactly what the word
  residual denotes, and it is why the classification stays not cleared even though
  every observed value on this side matches the pre-migration side.

DEFINITIONS EXPECTED, RE-DERIVED RATHER THAN ADOPTED
  Two command forms were run over this tree and both return 36.  The first is the
  plain form, a find for definition files with installed dependencies excluded.
  The second additionally prunes build-output and repository-metadata directories.
  They agree here because this working tree currently carries no build copies of
  definition resources; on a built tree the plain form would additionally count the
  build copies, which is a property of the working tree and not of the corpus.
  The breakdown is recorded so a reviewer can localise any shortfall rather than
  merely observe one, and the source set each figure belongs to is stated because
  it is what makes a difference explicable.
  complaint plugin                          1   main source
  task plugin                               5   3 main source, 2 test source
  personnel security plugin                 1   main source
  document management service               3   main source
  media engine service                      1   main source
  transcription service                     1   main source
  freedom-of-information application       11   main source
  privacy application                       8   main source
  workflow engine configuration module      5   test source
  TOTAL                                    36   29 main source, 7 test source
